<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23816" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-servo</span></b> , 1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To attend to</i>, <i>observe</i> (a
			favorite word of Statius): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemit, inservante noverca, Liber,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 10, 886</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volucres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 194</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6, 935</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To keep</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sagittae volitantes vires integras inservabant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 15, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
